{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>And of Benjamin he said: The beloved of HaShem shall dwell in safety by Him.</b> Since Jacob said: ״בִּנְיָמִן זְאֵב יִטְרָף בַּבֹּקֶר יֹאכַל עַד״ and so forth (Genesis 49:27), and one who tears prey does not eat it in security, for his heart pounds lest the one from whom he seized it come back upon him — therefore he said: ״יִשְׁכּוֹן לָבֶטַח עָלָיו״, and the word ״עָלָיו״ refers back to that spoil which Jacob mentioned. And since Jacob said: ״בַּבֹּקֶר יֹאכַל עַד וְלָעֶרֶב יְחַלֵּק שָׁלָל״, and the Targum explained that this refers to the offerings sacrificed morning and evening in the Temple situated in his portion — concerning this he added to say: ״חֹפֵף עָלָיו כָּל הַיּוֹם״, that it would not be destroyed like Shiloh and Nov and Giv'on, but rather the Shekhinah would always remain in its eternal abode. ״וּבֵין כְתֵפָיו שָׁכֵן״, for there the bearers of the ephod would be, for the Shekhinah was in the Urim and Tumim that the priest bore between his two shoulders; this is what it said: ״וּבֵין כְתֵפָיו שָׁכֵן״."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:16:34.254115275Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}